    "Description": "Mozilla Firefox is an open-source web browser, designed for standards compliance, performance, and portability.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* libexpat: denial of service via crafted XML input (CVE-2026-45186)\n\n* firefox: thunderbird: Privilege escalation in the Application Update component (CVE-2026-109704)\n\n* firefox: Use-after-free in the XML component (CVE-2026-109718)\n\n* firefox: Information disclosure in the PDF Viewer component (CVE-2026-109742)\n\n* firefox: Incorrect boundary conditions in the JavaScript Engine component (CVE-2026-109715)\n\n* firefox: firefox: Sandbox escape via incorrect boundary conditions in Win32 widget (CVE-2026-109740)\n\n* firefox: Use-after-free in the Storage: IndexedDB component (CVE-2026-109706)\n\n* firefox: Use-after-free in the Crash Reporting component (CVE-2026-109713)\n\n* firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Core \u0026 HTML component (CVE-2026-109724)\n\n* firefox: Sandbox escape due to uninitialized memory in the DOM: Web Serial component (CVE-2026-109745)\n\n* firefox: Mitigation bypass in the File Handling component (CVE-2026-109782)\n\n* firefox: Information disclosure, privilege escalation in the Security: Process Sandboxing component (CVE-2026-109709)\n\n* firefox: Sandbox escape, site isolation issue due to incorrect boundary conditions, use-after-free in the Networking component (CVE-2026-109705)\n\n* firefox: Use-after-free in the Audio/Video: Playback component (CVE-2026-109738)\n\n* firefox: Use-after-free in the Storage: Bucket File System component (CVE-2026-109741)\n\n* firefox: Use-after-free in the JavaScript Engine: JIT component (CVE-2026-109729)\n\n* firefox: Other issue in the DOM: File component (CVE-2026-109744)\n\n* firefox: Incorrect boundary conditions in the JavaScript Engine component (CVE-2026-109716)\n\n* firefox: Race condition, use-after-free in the Graphics: CanvasWebGL component (CVE-2026-109719)\n\n* firefox: Incorrect boundary conditions in the Layout component (CVE-2026-109753)\n\n* firefox: Integer overflow in the Layout: Text and Fonts component (CVE-2026-109723)\n\n* firefox: JIT miscompilation in the JavaScript Engine: JIT component (CVE-2026-109733)\n\n* firefox: Sandbox escape due to incorrect boundary conditions in the Networking component (CVE-2026-109708)\n\n* firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Bindings (WebIDL) component (CVE-2026-109717)\n\n* firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Workers component (CVE-2026-109752)\n\n* firefox: Sandbox escape due to use-after-free in the Networking component (CVE-2026-109707)\n\n* firefox: JIT miscompilation in the JavaScript: WebAssembly component (CVE-2026-109720)\n\n* firefox: Use-after-free in the SVG component (CVE-2026-109726)\n\n* firefox: Integer overflow in the Graphics component (CVE-2026-109730)\n\n* firefox: Use-after-free in the Audio/Video component (CVE-2026-109727)\n\n* firefox: Mitigation bypass in the Enterprise Policies component (CVE-2026-109737)\n\n* firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Streams component (CVE-2026-109732)\n\n* firefox: Information disclosure in the Networking component (CVE-2026-109751)\n\n* firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Core \u0026 HTML component (CVE-2026-109725)\n\n* firefox: Sandbox escape due to uninitialized memory in the Graphics component (CVE-2026-109712)\n\n* firefox: Use-after-free in the Graphics: Canvas2D component (CVE-2026-109711)\n\n* firefox: Frame poisoning in the Layout component (CVE-2026-109736)\n\n* firefox: JIT miscompilation in the JavaScript Engine: JIT component (CVE-2026-109722)\n\n* firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Animation component (CVE-2026-109728)\n\n* firefox: Incorrect boundary conditions in the JavaScript Engine: JIT component (CVE-2026-109721)\n\n* firefox: Privilege escalation in the Panning and Zooming component (CVE-2026-109743)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Firefox ESR 153 rebase [rhel-8.10.z] (JIRA:RHEL-175143)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
